{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2021-1013","published":"2021-02-04T11:04:14Z","modified":"2026-08-18T01:15:14.026180018Z","upstream":["CVE-2019-25013"],"summary":"glibc security update","details":"The GNU C Library project provides the core libraries for the GNU system and GNU/Linux systems, as well as many other systems that use Linux as the kernel. These libraries provide critical APIs including ISO C11, POSIX.1-2008, BSD, OS-specific APIs and more. These APIs include such foundational facilities as open, read, write, malloc, printf, getaddrinfo, dlopen, pthread_create, crypt,  login, exit and more.\\r\\n\\r\\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\\r\\n\\r\\n\r\nThe iconv feature in the GNU C Library (aka glibc or libc6) through 2.32, when processing invalid multi-byte input sequences in the EUC-KR encoding, may have a buffer over-read.(CVE-2019-25013)\\r\\n\\r\\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"glibc","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/glibc&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.28-52.oe1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["nscd-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-locale-source-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-nss-devel-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-debugutils-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-benchtests-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-devel-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-common-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-debuginfo-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-debugsource-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","libnsl-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","nss_modules-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-all-langpacks-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","nscd-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-locale-source-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-nss-devel-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-debugutils-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-benchtests-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-devel-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-common-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-debuginfo-2.28-52.oe1.aarch64.rpm","glibc-debugsource-2.28-52.oe1.aarch6